<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2d0d4729-993d-5993-885d-688dfb11e6e0" activityNameId="eacab5f0-015d-538b-b834-d80f49d1d18c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Separator, lithium-ion battery, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Separator, lithium-ion battery, at plant
The dataset can be used as a seperator membrane between a cathode and an anode, e.g. for a lithium-ion battery. Data are based on patents. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.;
UUID: 1e15c5f4-d81a-35a2-b262-e495f647b22d
This dataset incudes the production of a seperator for a lithium-ion battery. Polyethylene foil is coated with a slurry composed of silica, a Co-polymere of  PVDF (proxy: PVF) and hexafluor ethane and dibutyl phthalate (proxy: phthalic anhydride). The polytehylene foil is coated on 1 side with the slurry. Then, the coated foil is dried in a "dry channel" (H2O content &lt; 20 ppm) and coiled up. The same procedure is done for the second side of the collector foil.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: This dataset includes a method of producing a seperator for a lithium ion battery. The seperator seperates anode from cathode, but allows an exchange of Li+-ions through micropores. In case of to high process temperature of the battery, the seperator melts,  thus  closes the micopores, interrupts the Li+-ion exchange and therefore stops the chemical process and pretends finally from  overheating or a burning battery . 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: patent, website, ecoinvent 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1e15c5f4-d81a-35a2-b262-e495f647b22d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3142d8e2-0d30-557e-b090-9faae2b72357" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CN</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: &lt;null&gt;</text>
